%% title: Control flow: one deploy call through the crates
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CI as deploy job
    participant H as http-api
    participant D as service-app Deploy
    participant R as rollout decider
    participant E as adapter-postgres
    participant Q as composition queue
    participant C as compiler compose
    participant K as adapter-kube
    participant V as adapter-vault
    participant G as adapter-ghcr
    CI->>H: POST /deploys (OIDC token, fragment digest)
    H->>H: claim policy, then route policy
    H->>D: run(DeployCommand)
    D->>E: events of this rollout
    E-->>D: events
    D->>R: decide(state, Deploy)
    R-->>D: Accepted events, or a Refusal
    D->>E: append events
    D->>Q: submit trigger
    Q->>C: compose(pinned inputs), blocking thread
    C->>C: read, link, check#59; lower#59; compose#59; resolve#59; render#59; serialize
    C-->>Q: renders and diagnostics per Project
    opt a fragment is refused
        Q->>E: append Refused for that Project#59; the others go on
    end
    Q->>K: server-side dry-run of every changed object
    K-->>Q: diagnostics, or clean
    alt the dry-run reports problems
        Q->>E: append Refused, with the diagnostics
    else the dry-run is clean
        opt the render's digest differs from the tag's
            Q->>V: sign the digest with the render key
            Q->>G: push the render
            Q->>K: take the writer Lease
            Q->>G: move render/#lt#59;p#gt#59;:prod by compare-and-swap
        end
        Q->>E: append Published or Unchanged
    end
    H-->>CI: stream events over SSE, resumable by sequence
